{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>answered</b>: \"In truth I know that you are buying time.\" The meaning: you are stalling the moment because you see that a word goes out from my mouth and it stands. That is: if you do not tell me the dream, your law is one — the law that I have given, that you shall be killed. And the dalet of הזדמנתון stands in place of the tav of the hitpa'el. And R. Marinus said: for thus the word הזכו is like הזדכו. But it cannot be nif'al because of the dagesh in the kaf. And R. Moses the Kohen Sephardi said: it is hitpa'el, and the dagesh in the zayin is because the tav is swallowed; it is התזכו, and this is the correct one in my eyes."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The lemma reads 'answered' (ענה) though Daniel 2:8 begins with ענה מלך ('the king answered'); Ibn Ezra apparently lemmatizes on the verb alone. R. Marinus and R. Moses the Kohen Sephardi are cited by name; the former's name is a transliterated Latin/Greek form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:19:06.837071820Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}